getStackHeight [SimTalk] - Store
Returns the height of the stack in meters on the designated storage place in the Store designated by
<Path>.
Remarks
getStackHeight also applies to places on pallets/Containers and to Transporters with a loading space of
type Store.
Note
Here the height of the stack designates its physical height, not the number of parts on the stack.
If you output the value with the method print, the unit is the unit you selected under Preferences/
Model Settings > Unit > Length.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.pe(X:integer, Y:integer).getStackHeight → length
<Path>[X:integer, Y:integer].getStackHeight → length
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter X of data type integer designates the position of the storage place (on the production
element) in the X-Dimension.
• The parameter Y of data type integer designates the position of the storage place (on the production
element) in the Y-Dimension.
Return Value
The return value has the data type length.
Example
print MyStore.pe(2,1).getStackHeight
print MyStore[2,1].getStackHeight
